{"adjusted_volatile_messages": [["user","Prepare the requested reusable draft without executing any operation."]], "bridge_messages": [], "composition_summary": "Drafted one unapproved pure-logic class-22 component for pc-contrast-07. The observed witness showed explicit null returning {'ok': False, 'records': None}; the contract requires [] in every invalid outcome. The body uses a helper that receives the whole inputs mapping to distinguish absent from explicit null, and assigns its returned object to module-level result. No I/O, imports, host calls or upstream validation assumption. No execution, submission, Q1/Q2 or activation was performed by this example reviewer.", "proposed_components": [{"class_code": 22, "payload": {"name": "pc-contrast-07", "description": "Raw records is a list of 1..3 items. Every object has exactly code and enabled, code string length 2..5 inclusive, enabled exact bool (False valid). Always result={ok:boolean,records:original if valid else []}. Empty is invalid; missing/null/wrong types/extra fields invalid without exceptions/coercion. No I/O/imports/host calls, no upstream validation assumption. Target typed inputs interface requires selected-runner support; unapproved draft, not submitted or activated.", "content": "def inspect_records(mapping):
